/*
A while loop in JavaScript is used to repeatedly execute a block of code
as long as a given condition is true. The condition is checked before
each iteration, so if it’s false initially, the loop won’t run at all.
It’s commonly used when the number of iterations is not known in advance,
such as reading input or processing data until a condition changes.
*/
// syntax
/*
while(condition){

    block of code

}
*/

/*
A for loop in JavaScript runs a block of code a fixed number of times
 using initialization, condition, and update in one line.

*/

/*
    Syntax

for (initialization; condition; update) {
    // code to execute
}

*/

/*
    for…in
Used to loop over keys/indexes of an object or array.

for (let key in obj) {
  // use obj[key]
}


for…of
Used to loop over values of iterable objects (arrays, strings).

for (let value of arr) {
  // use value
}


forEach
An array method that runs a function for each element.

arr.forEach((value, index) => {
  // use value and index
});

*/
